<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
Norwegian Bokmål (nb-NO) — full UI coverage matching the German reference.
Register: informal "du" throughout. Brand name "ClothesCast" stays verbatim.

What is NOT overridden, by design:
- `app_name` — brand identifier, identical across locales.
- `insight_time_am` / `_pm` / `_midnight` / `_noon` (and *_minutes variants)
  — English-only spoken-time formatter helpers. Norwegian uses
  `insight_time_hour` / `insight_time_hour_minutes` ("%1$d" / "%1$d:%2$02d")
  with "klokken" from surrounding templates.

`settings_region_language_*` and `settings_tts_voice_locale_*` use Norwegian
native names for all locales (e.g. "Tysk (Tyskland)", "Fransk (Frankrike)").
-->
